{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent positive bias: forecasts are systematically too high vs. realized prices, especially beyond ~day 10; apply a downward level shift (increasing with horizon).",
    "Underestimates downside momentum: during selloffs the model reverts upward too quickly; incorporate stronger negative trend continuation / slower mean reversion after declines.",
    "Horizon-dependent overshoot: errors grow with lead time (small early, large late). Use a horizon-based shrinkage toward a lower path (e.g., progressively larger haircut after day ~7–10).",
    "Fails to capture step-down regimes: when the market transitions to a lower band, the model stays anchored to the prior regime; add a regime-switch/rolling-anchor rule (re-anchor to recent 5–10 day mean when new lows are made).",
    "Peaks/bumps are too strong and too late: forecasted rebounds/mini-spikes (around mid-horizon) exceed realized and appear lagged; dampen rebound amplitude and advance/diffuse turning points (reduce curvature)."
  ]
}
